WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Pressure over a bony prominence can compress the local

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.720
capillary bed.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.700
Watch flow diminish as the tissue is compressed.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.218
Unrelieved pressure reduces oxygen
delivery and can cause ischemia

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.138
and necrosis.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.840
Depth matters: injury can extend from skin into deeper

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.757
supporting tissues.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.420
Pressure relief and repositioning
address the initiating force.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.780
An intact red surface and an exposed deep wound

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.640
represent different findings; a
covered wound base may prevent

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.197
staging.
